Steps :
> mkdir manggo-api
> cd manggo-api/

> npm init
	- description: APIs for MangGo App
	- entry point: (index.js) app.js
	- author: Adit
	- the rests yes

> git init
> copy .gitignore from other api project


> npm install --save express

Cors handler (express middleware) :
- npm install --save cors

For Logger, use Pino (instead of morgan) :
- npm install --save pino pino-http
- npm install --save-dev pino-pretty

For input validations :
- npm install --save express-validator
	detail docs of validation: https://github.com/validatorjs/validator.js/blob/master/README.md

Install Prisma :
	- npm install prisma@6 --save-dev
	- npm install --save @prisma/client@6

Setup schema.prisma file including DB-name within .env file, then:
	- npx prisma migrate dev --name init


Cloudinary Setup (Cloud-based image service):
	- npm install --save cloudinary


============================================
[Deployment]

Deploy schema based on historical migrations
- npx prisma migrate deploy


To monitor all running status:
- node monitor.js


============================================
[Data structure]

model sessions {
  id        String   @id @default(uuid())   // sessionId

  contents  contents[]

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt
}

model contents {
  id              String  @id @default(cuid())
  prompt          String
  style           String?
  originalPrompt  String?

  imageUrl      String?     // Cloudinary URL
  status        String      // queueing / generating / uploading / success / failed
  error         String?     // error string when failed

  sessionId     String
  session       sessions  @relation(fields: [sessionId], references: [id])

  createdAt     DateTime  @default(now())

  @@unique([id, sessionId])
}



In order to give better UX for meaningful loading states at FE (10-30s is normal), here are the status to set:

Status:
	pending - request_received ("Pending request"):
		user submit, backend set "pending" state.

	processing:
		generating_image ("Generating AI image"): request pass to AI to generate image
		uploading_image ("Uploading image"): after image returned from AI, upload image to Cloudinary

	success - done: if AI and cloudinary upload success, set success.

	failed - done: if one of AI or cloudinary upload failed, set failed and set error for reason.



===========================================
[To Pollinations AI API]

API GET IMAGE:
	https://gen.pollinations.ai/image/${encodedPrompt}?model=flux
	headers: {
		Authorization: 'Bearer YOUR_SECRET_TOKEN'
	}

return image file.

